  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 5 \\\\ t & 9\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$",
  "worked_solution": "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 9-t\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =9t-5t \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$",
